// A snapshot of every item the game knows about, taken before play begins. Any
// save written before an item existed has no key for it, and loading such a save
// used to leave the key UNDEFINED rather than 0 — at which point every `<1`
// guard silently fails, because `undefined < 1` is false. That is how Eldan
// stopped handing over the sacred scroll and the kindness trial became
// unfinishable, with nothing thrown and nothing logged.
// Filled by a late pass, NOT here: seeds, potions and bread are added to the
// inventory further down the file, so a snapshot taken at this line would miss
